    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nI use jkl; (home-row) keys to move around instead of hjkl, so I need to remap the down/up keys to k/l. As it is, mini.files doesn't provide a way to remap them.\r\n\r\nI read the source code but wasn't able to figure out where mini.files sets j/k or where it inherit those remaps from.\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to add those remaps?",
    "closed_at": "2023-11-30T08:39:11Z",
