        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Buffers in 'mini.files' explorer are regular buffers with local mappings controlled by `config.mappings`. It means that global mappings have effect in those buffers too *if* it is not overshadowed by buffer-local one.\r\n\r\nHere is a minimal setup to have `k`/`l` working in this use case:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.files').setup({ mappings = { go_in = ';', go_out = 'j' } })\r\nvim.keymap.set({ 'n', 'x', 'o' }, 'k', '<Down>')\r\nvim.keymap.set({ 'n', 'x', 'o' }, 'l', '<Up>')\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2023-11-30T08:39:12Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/596#issuecomment-1833322835",
